In this episode, we re-examine some of the Lenape villages and the Norweigian forts. Then we build a big earthen fort, while I talk a little bit about the American Revolution. Then I tell you about a trip I took a while back to study democracy.

Note to copyright guys: the music is a public domain recording of Edvard Greig's "Morning Mood" from Musopen -- I did not steal your music. You can see for yourself here: https://musopen.org/music/777-peer-gynt-suite-no-1-op-46/


The title music is Beethoven's Symphony no. 5 in Cm, Op. 67 - IV. Allegro, performed by the Davis High School Symphony Orchestra. This is also public domain music from Musopen: https://musopen.org/music/2567-symphony-no-5-in-cm-op-67/

